//? Title: Generational collection: retain the young across an old boundary
//? Subtitle: Actual graph traces, conservative floating garbage and a maintained reference-write barrier
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Identify young objects that can be reclaimed while leaving old objects outside
the collected generation. References from old to young objects must still protect
their targets, including young descendants reached through those targets.
This report follows the native collector’s actual events, reproduces the original
seven-object example and distinguishes young-object visits from total work.
A conservative boundary can retain young garbage that a full trace would reject.
A second native heap model maintains exact old-to-young slots on checked writes,
allowing sparse young-only analysis after setup. All results describe graph
candidates: no real objects, ages or memory are changed by collection.
)

\toc

> A rooted old object can protect a young object

Object 0 is old and rooted. Its one field points to young object 1, while young
object 2 is isolated. The minor analysis records old source 0, marks young target 1,
visits 1, proposes its promotion and lists 2 as a reclamation candidate. It does
not need to traverse the old source during the young marking phase. The legacy
API nevertheless pays for old-field discovery and a separate full comparison.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/generation_first.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/generational.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const dm::algorithms::ObjectGraph g{3,{{1},{},{}},{0},{}};const std::vector<int>ages{1,0,0};const auto t=dm::algorithms::minor_gc_trace(g,ages,0);
 std::print("| actual event | source or object | target | accepted | stack size |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: |\n");
 for(const auto&e:t.events)if(e.kind=="old_field"||e.kind=="remember"||e.kind=="visit"||e.kind=="promote"||e.kind=="free")std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",e.kind,e.object,e.target,e.accepted,e.stack_size);
 std::print("\nRetained young {}; full-root live {}; remembered source {}; freed candidate {}; inspected old fields {}; validation fields {}.\n",t.run.result.minor_scanned,t.run.result.full_scanned,t.run.result.remembered_set.at(0),t.run.result.young_freed.at(0),t.run.work.old_fields,t.run.work.validation.references);
 dm::graphics::Diagram d(62,1050);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle old,young,dead;old.width=4.7;old.height=2.1;old.font_size=22;old.fill={241,245,249};young=old;young.fill={219,234,254};dead=old;dead.fill={255,237,213};
 d.node("old",{0,0},std::format("Rooted OLD source {}\nfield points into young",t.run.result.remembered_set[0]),old)
  .node("young",{6.3,0},std::format("YOUNG object {}\nretained through boundary",1),young)
  .node("garbage",{6.3,-3.2},std::format("YOUNG object {}\nunreached: free candidate",t.run.result.young_freed[0]),dead)
  .edge("old","young","boundary")
  .text({3.1,2.5},"Minor tracing stops at old objects but preserves their young targets",24).save_svg("build/generation_first.svg");
 if(t.run.result.promoted!=std::vector<char>{0,1,0}||t.run.result.young_freed!=std::vector<int>{2})throw std::runtime_error("boundary toy example");
}
```
