Young visits 2; full visits 6; remembered source 3; old fields inspected 4; full fields inspected 4; validation references 4; dense promotion slots 7; legacy result identical true.
\image(figures/generation_original.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The original output is preserved: two young visits, six full-root visits, survivor proposals 4 and 5, free candidate 6 and remembered source 3. Total work also includes validation, boundary discovery, dense output and full tracing.)
\alttext(Four rooted old-chain objects lead to young 5. Young 4 is directly rooted and young 6 isolated. Computed marks distinguish old full-root liveness from young retention proposals.)

Safety does not require the minor result to equal full-root liveness. If a full
root-to-young path contains no old object, its entire path begins at a young root
and lies in G[Y]. Otherwise take its last old-to-young crossing: that target is in
B, and the remaining suffix contains only young objects. Therefore

$$
\operatorname{Reach}_{G}(R)\cap Y\ \subseteq\ M.
$$
\alttext(Every young object reachable from a real root is retained by the conservative minor analysis, but the retained set may be larger.)

This proves retention safety for the graph model, including paths that pass
through old objects between young segments. It does not prove that all retained
young objects are truly live, or that a candidate is physically freed.

> An unreachable old source can preserve floating garbage

Now remove all roots from old 0→young 1→young 2. A full trace reaches nothing.
A conservative minor collection still treats old 0 as a boundary source and
retains young 1 and 2. This is floating garbage: young objects survive this minor
analysis even though a full collection could reclaim the entire component.
Remembered-set membership is evidence of an old-to-young field, not of the old
source’s root reachability. Minor retention can consequently exceed full liveness.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/generation_floating.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/generational.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 dm::algorithms::ObjectGraph g{3,{{1},{2},{}},{0},{}};const std::vector<int>ages{1,0,0};
 std::array<double,2>minor{},full{};std::print("| configuration | root slots | young visits | full-root visits | retained young without root path |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
 for(std::size_t k=0;k<2;++k){if(k)g.roots.clear();const auto r=dm::algorithms::minor_gc_run(g,ages);std::size_t floating=0;for(std::size_t i=0;i<ages.size();++i)if(r.result.promoted[i]&&!r.full_reachable[i])++floating;minor[k]=r.result.minor_scanned;full[k]=r.result.full_scanned;
  std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",k?"No roots":"Rooted old source",g.roots.size(),r.result.minor_scanned,r.result.full_scanned,floating);}
 auto rooted=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({minor[0],full[0]},{"Minor young","Full-root"});rooted.title("Rooted old source").xlab("").ylab("Objects visited").y_limits(0,4);
 auto unrooted=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({minor[1],full[1]},{"Minor young","Full-root"});unrooted.title("Unreachable old source").xlab("").ylab("Objects visited").y_limits(0,4);
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(rooted).add(unrooted).size(1100,500).title("Conservative young retention can outlive root reachability").fit_panels().save_svg("build/generation_floating.svg");
 if(minor[1]!=2||full[1]!=0)throw std::runtime_error("floating young garbage");
}
