\caption(The no-roots case visits two young objects but zero full-root objects. This is permitted conservative retention, so “a minor collection always visits fewer objects” is false.)
\alttext(Two panels compare minor/full visits 2/3 for a rooted source and 2/0 after removing every root. The table identifies two retained young objects lacking any root path.)

> Maintain remembered slots at the actual write boundary

The new heap model owns its graph, fixed binary ages, a sparse young-id table and
an exact ordered set of old-to-young (source,field) slots. Checked set_reference
replaces an existing field and updates that one slot’s membership. Two fields from
the same source are distinct entries; changing one must not erase the other.
Replacing a young target with an old one removes that slot. Writing through a
young source never creates an old-to-young entry.

This invariant is preserved locally because ages and field counts are fixed:
only the replaced slot can change category. A new set node is allocated before
the graph changes, so invalid indices or failed insertion leave the model intact.
Ordered-set maintenance costs O(log(W+1)) per replacement for W boundary slots.
This is a modeled write barrier, not a claim about runtime machine instructions.
The model deliberately does not apply the collector’s promotion proposals: changing
ages would require rebuilding or updating the boundary index under a separate API.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/generation_barrier.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/generational.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const dm::algorithms::ObjectGraph g{4,{{0,0},{2},{},{}},{0},{}};const std::vector<int>ages{1,0,0,1};dm::algorithms::GenerationalHeap heap(g,ages);
 const std::array<std::array<int,2>,4>writes{{{0,1},{1,2},{0,3},{1,3}}};std::vector<double>step,slots,survivors;
 std::print("| step | replaced field | new target | boundary after write | remembered slots | retained young | free candidates | old fields scanned by collect |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
 for(std::size_t k=0;k<=writes.size();++k){int field=-1,target=-1;bool tracked=false;if(k){field=writes[k-1][0];target=writes[k-1][1];tracked=heap.set_reference(0,field,target);}const auto r=heap.collect();const auto check=dm::algorithms::minor_gc(heap.snapshot(),ages);
  std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",k,field,target,tracked,r.work.remembered_fields,r.survivors.size(),r.freed.size(),r.work.old_fields);step.push_back(k);slots.push_back(r.work.remembered_fields);survivors.push_back(r.survivors.size());
  if(r.survivors.size()!=std::size_t(check.minor_scanned)||r.freed!=check.young_freed||heap.remembered_sources()!=check.remembered_set)throw std::runtime_error("maintained barrier versus explicit rebuilt check");}
 std::print("\nConstructor old-field checks {}; current remembered sources {}; original first field {}; model final first field {}.\n",heap.preparation_work().old_fields,heap.remembered_sources().size(),g.refs[0][0],heap.snapshot().refs[0][0]);
 auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();plot.lines(step,slots,"Remembered slots",{37,99,235},2).points(step,slots,"",{37,99,235},6)
  .lines(step,survivors,"Retained young",{220,38,38},2).points(step,survivors,"",{220,38,38},6).legend({"Remembered slots","Retained young"},{{37,99,235},{220,38,38}})
  .title("Checked writes maintain exact boundary slots without an old-field rescan").xlab("Write number; zero is the initial model").ylab("Slots or young objects, distinct counted units").y_limits(-.1,3.2).size(1100,540).save_svg("build/generation_barrier.svg");
}
```
