// result_end
\caption(Initial field/target−1 values mean no write yet. The explicit snapshot-and-rebuild call is a separate correctness check; its copy/full-trace cost is excluded from the sparse collect counters shown. Caller input remains unchanged.)
\alttext(Four writes produce remembered-slot counts 0,1,2,1,0 and young-survivor counts 0,2,2,1,0. Collect inspects zero old fields at every stage; duplicate source fields retain independent memberships.)

> Separate paid setup from repeated young-only work

For the legacy API, complete validation checks the whole graph and ages. Boundary
discovery tests every object and scans old fields; the collector then marks young
objects, constructs dense output and runs a full-root comparison. Its total is
O(N+E+R), with N objects, E fields and R root slots. The two-visit number in the
original example does not describe this total cost.

The maintained model pays O(N+E+R) construction once and stores the graph/index.
Each collect then needs

$$
T_{\mathrm{collect}}=O(Y+R+W+E_y),
$$
\alttext(A maintained collection visits the young-id table, root slots, remembered old-to-young slots and fields of retained young objects, rather than all old objects.)

Here Y is the number of young objects, W the exact remembered slots, and E_y
fields of retained young objects, including their old targets. It initializes
only Y marks and returns sparse young ids, avoiding a dense N-entry result.
The explicit graph snapshot method copies the whole graph; it is not part of this
bound. Constructors, checked writes and any separate full comparison must still
be accounted for. A large W or many surviving young fields can make a minor
collection expensive even with few young objects.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/generation_scaling.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/generational.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 std::vector<double>x,eager_y,maintained_y;std::print("| old objects | eager old fields | eager full visits | setup old fields | maintained slots | maintained young visits | maintained young classifications |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
 for(std::size_t old:std::array<std::size_t,9>{1,2,4,8,16,64,256,1024,4096}){const auto input=dm::algorithms::generational_chain_example(old);const auto eager=dm::algorithms::minor_gc_run(input.graph,input.generations);dm::algorithms::GenerationalHeap heap(input.graph,input.generations);const auto young=heap.collect();
  std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",old,eager.work.old_fields,eager.work.full_objects,heap.preparation_work().old_fields,young.work.remembered_fields,young.work.young_objects,young.work.classified_young);x.push_back(std::log2(double(old)));eager_y.push_back(std::log2(double(eager.work.old_fields)));maintained_y.push_back(std::log2(double(young.work.remembered_fields)));
  if(eager.result.minor_scanned!=2||young.work.remembered_fields!=1||young.work.old_fields||young.work.full_objects||young.work.validation.rows||young.work.dense_result_slots||young.work.classified_young!=3)throw std::runtime_error("sparse boundary scaling");}
 auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();plot.lines(x,eager_y,"Rebuilt old fields",{37,99,235},2).points(x,eager_y,"",{37,99,235},5)
  .lines(x,maintained_y,"Maintained slots",{5,150,105},2).points(x,maintained_y,"",{5,150,105},5).legend({"Rebuilt old fields","Maintained slots"},{{37,99,235},{5,150,105}})
  .title("Old-chain growth: rebuilt discovery grows; maintained boundary stays at one").xlab("log2 old-chain length").ylab("log2 actual fields or slots examined").y_limits(-1,16).size(1100,560).save_svg("build/generation_scaling.svg");
}
