\caption(Three young ids and one old-to-young slot remain fixed while the old chain grows. Setup and eager full tracing grow with it; repeated maintained collection visits two surviving young objects and classifies three young ids.)
\alttext(A log-base-two plot shows eager old-field discovery growing from 1 to 4096 while maintained boundary-slot visits stay 1. The table separately records constructor work and eager full visits.)

These are counted graph operations, not timings, instruction counts or measured
runtime pause reductions. The examples test a chosen age partition and reference
pattern; they do not establish an empirical survival distribution. Sizes are
ignored because this model counts object slots, not bytes.

> Validation, ownership and resource units remain explicit

Complete graph/id and exact binary-age validation precede every eager analysis,
including trivial/empty outcomes and trace quota checks. The maintained model
validates before copying/indexing and admits only checked existing-field writes.
This closes the original unchecked short-age, high-root, high-child and short-row
accesses. Ages other than 0 or 1 are rejected rather than silently omitting an object
from both categories. Slot-based collection still ignores all size metadata.

The trace checks each actual primitive record online: default one million,
zero disables only that optional quota. Records are not numeric entries or bytes,
and this is not a peak RAM limit. Owned input vectors, root/work metadata, final
ordinary output, working tables/stacks and allocator storage are excluded. No
partial trace, truncation, numerical replay or caller mutation is returned on
quota failure. The family generator uses a separate whole-object bound before
allocation; one original seven-object example requires cap 7 and rejects 6.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/generation_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/generational.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const dm::algorithms::ObjectGraph one{1,{{}},{0},{}};const auto observed=dm::algorithms::minor_gc_trace(one,{0},0);bool trace_denied=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::minor_gc_trace(one,{0},7);}catch(const std::length_error&){trace_denied=true;}
 auto t=dm::algorithms::minor_gc_trace(one,{0},8);t.graph.refs[0].push_back(0);t.generations[0]=1;t.events[0].kind="changed";const bool owned=t.run.result.promoted[0]&&t.events[1].kind=="seed"&&t.run.full_reachable[0];
 bool objects_denied=false,ages_first=false,shape_first=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::generational_chain_example(4,1,6);}catch(const std::length_error&){objects_denied=true;}const auto input=dm::algorithms::generational_chain_example(4,1,7);
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::minor_gc_trace({2,{{1},{}},{0},{}},{2,0},1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){ages_first=true;}try{(void)dm::algorithms::minor_gc_trace({2,{{99},{}},{0},{}},{1,0},1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){shape_first=true;}
 dm::algorithms::GenerationalHeap heap({2,{{0},{}},{0},{}},{1,0});const auto before=heap.snapshot().refs;bool invalid_write=false;try{(void)heap.set_reference(0,0,2);}catch(const std::out_of_range&){invalid_write=true;}const bool atomic=invalid_write&&heap.snapshot().refs==before;
 const auto empty=dm::algorithms::minor_gc_trace({},{},1);
 std::print("| resource | observed or required | admitted or copied | rejected cap | rejection observed |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| Actual event records | {} | {} | 7 | {} |\n| Whole generated objects | 7 | {} | 6 | {} |\n",observed.events.size(),t.events.size(),trace_denied,input.graph.num_objects,objects_denied);
 std::print("\nIndependent owned trace copies {}; invalid ages before quota {}; invalid graph before quota {}; invalid write leaves model unchanged {}; empty events {}; empty young visits {}; empty full visits {}.\n",owned,ages_first,shape_first,atomic,empty.events.size(),empty.run.result.minor_scanned,empty.run.result.full_scanned);
 auto events=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(observed.events.size()),double(t.events.size()),7.},{"Observed","Admitted","Rejected cap"});events.title("Online primitive records").xlab("").ylab("Complete event records").y_limits(0,10);
 auto objects=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({7.,double(input.graph.num_objects),6.},{"Required","Created","Rejected cap"});objects.title("Whole generated graph").xlab("").ylab("Objects, not bytes").y_limits(0,10);
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(events).add(objects).size(1100,500).title("Actual trace capture and known-size graph admission use different units").fit_panels().save_svg("build/generation_controls.svg");
 if(!trace_denied||!objects_denied||!owned||!ages_first||!shape_first||!atomic||!empty.events.empty())throw std::runtime_error("validation, ownership and quota controls");
}
