\caption(The singleton run contains eight actual events; cap 7 rejects the next record and cap 8 admits it. The generated original graph independently needs seven object slots. Neither quota is a memory-byte guarantee.)
\alttext(Two panels show event records 8 observed,8 admitted and 7 rejected, and graph objects 7 required,7 created and 6 rejected. Computed flags verify validation precedence, independent snapshots and atomic invalid writes.)

The original result survives unchanged, while its interpretation becomes more
precise: two young visits coexist with whole-graph discovery and comparison work.
The sparse maintained model makes write-side bookkeeping explicit and avoids that
repeated old scan under a fixed age partition. Conservative retention protects
all root-reachable young objects but can preserve floating garbage. These graph
invariants, actual traces and selected operation counts explain the method without
claiming a complete runtime collector or universal generational performance.
